  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Multisector Support Programme for Displaced and Vulnerable Conflict and Crisis Affected Populations in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the mass displacements in Sudan continue to increase due to the ongoing armed conflict between the Sudanese Armed Forces (SAF) and Rapid Support Forces (RSF), IOM is addressing critical humanitarian needs by providing integrated multisector support for vulnerable conflict and crisis-affected populations across the country including internally displaced persons (IDPs), refugees, returnees, and host communities. The main focus areas of the action are: coordination and support to humanitarian operations including continual operation of the common pipeline system and support for local partners to provide assistance to affected populations, strengthening localization; information management and monitoring via the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) on human mobility including internal displacement, return, and cross-border movements, as well as conflict sensitivity analysis; and shelters and distribution of essential non-food items in coordination with relevant clusters, United Nations agencies, local partners, and authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
